WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.819
This is the St Francis Dam, outside Los Angeles.
Or rather, what's left of it. More than 50

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:10.500
metres high, holding back 100,000 tonnes of
water. Until it collapsed catastrophically

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.320
in 1928, twelve hours after its chief engineer
had said that the cracks in it weren't anything

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.029
to be worried about.

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:21.560
The chief engineer in question was William
Mulholland. He's one of the reasons that LA

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:26.949
is the size and scale it is: Mulholland Drive,
home of the stars, is named after him, and

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:32.070
his career before the dam collapse was astonishing.
He was in charge of projects that diverted

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.980
a river, and caused what became known as the
California Water Wars, as locals tried to

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.910
dynamite and destroy the infrastructure that
was pulling all the water away from their

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:46.260
farms. At the opening ceremony of the Los
Angeles Aqueduct, close to here, as water

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.879
cascaded down towards the growing city, Mulholland
declared to the mayor of Los Angeles: "there

00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:57.850
it is, take it". And they did. Remember, Los
Angeles was just one small city among many

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:02.649
in the valley at that point -- but its charter
didn't allow it to provide surplus water to

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:07.750
anyone else, so the only way for other cities
nearby to get access to this was to give up

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.220
their independence and become part of LA.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:14.909
And that might have continued, perhaps Burbank,
Pasadena, Anaheim, other cities that have

00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:21.040
separate local government today might all
be part of one enormous city... if it wasn't

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.030
for the St Francis Dam.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:27.920
The leading theory for the collapse is that
the foundations were unsound: on solid bedrock,

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.689
the dam would have been perfectly safe -- but
it was built on permeable ground, so the weight

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:37.310
of water held behind the dam started to seep
through and soften the ground under it. There

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:41.030
had always been a couple of cracks in the
dam; that was normal for the time, concrete

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:46.810
can do that as it sets. But more had started
to appear, leaks were starting to grow. Mulholland

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:51.310
and his assistant inspected the dam, and decided
that it needed maintenance, but the situation

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.649
wasn't desperate.

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:58.520
Well, maintenance couldn't have helped: the
dam was twelve hours away from collapse. But

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:03.840
evacuation of the areas below could have saved
hundreds of lives. Just before midnight, it

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.149
gave way catastrophically.

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:09.450
And as the courts of inquiry delivered their
verdicts, and as the last standing parts of

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:14.480
the dam were demolished and cleared to stop
sightseers and people taking grisly souvenirs,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.560
the cities that hadn't been eaten up by LA
yet: Beverly Hills, Santa Monica, plenty of

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.060
others -- decided that Los Angeles couldn't
be trusted with its water projects. They all

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.430
refused to join, and instead they formed what
was called a "Water District" with LA -- they

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:33.170
took joint control of any projects like that
in future. The dam collapse didn't just end

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:38.030
Mulholland's career: it ended the assimilation
of other cities into LA. We might talk about

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:42.319
the urban sprawl, everything in the valley,
as being Los Angeles, but it's not: it's separate

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:47.810
towns and separate goverements, and one of
the reasons is this valley and the dam that

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.310
isn't there any more.

